<title>UK: NWE naphtha steady, market balanced.</title>
<headline>NWE naphtha steady, market balanced.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE naphtha was stable on Friday with various pieces seen on offer but limited immediate buying, traders said.</p>
<p>Fixed price talk was in short supply.</p>
<p>A Greek cargo was heard available from a trader. This follows the movement of a Greek cargo offered earlier by another trader to the U.S.</p>
<p>One player said he thought Moroccan material was actively being offered, but a late-month Skikda held by a trader was not in view.</p>
<p>-- Nicholas Shaxson, London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
